OL,3,A'Quiet quitting' could be hitting the
OL,4,Aeconomy - here's why
OL,5,
OL,6,F"This is self-evidently bad for
OL,7,Fworkers, but it also doesn't bode well
OL,8,Ffor productivity and labour supply,
OL,9,Fboth of which are vital for lifting
OL,10,Fliving standards in the years ahead,"
OL,11,Fsaid Hannah Slaughter, principal
OL,12,Feconomist at the Resolution Foundation.
